{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_nnfxefjffydd54katyuifdx76apsdovs2nap4jveqqhs4g42ou6q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src` is a single tiny translation unit: `void driver(int floors)` fills a `house_t {int floors; int bedrooms; double bathrooms;}` with `{floors, 3, 2.0}` and hexdumps its 16 raw bytes to `stdout` via a `static` helper. One public symbol, no options, no error returns.\n\n## Phase A — artifacts (`translation/`)\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — C `.so` exports exactly one symbol (`T driver`); Rust `.so` exports exactly `T driver`. Diff is empty; nothing was missing, so no untranslated module and no stubs were needed. `print_hex`/`house_t` are `static`/file-local and correctly stay unexported on both sides.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 13 rows. Mechanical grep found **zero** rejection branches: no `return` at all (both functions are `void`), no `assert`, no null/range check, no `errno`, no error enum. The rows are therefore the generic boundaries (`0`, `INT_MAX`, `INT_MIN`, `-1`, unsigned `0x80000000`/`0xFFFFFFFF` pushed across the ABI, out-of-range \"enum-like\" ints) whose correct C result is *not an error*, plus rows documenting why `print_hex`'s `len<=0`/`NULL` cases and null/length arguments are structurally unreachable through the ABI.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 24 rows: no runtime flags exist, so the axes are input bit-pattern shapes (walking ones/zeros, per-byte exhaustive sweeps, high-bit bytes, low-nibble bytes, interior zeros, extremes, constant collisions) crossed with call-count/order/interleaving axes.\n\n## Phases B–D — results\n\nAll **41 cases pass** (24 valid-path, 13 error-path, 4 symbol-parity), across **4 configurations** (default × `--no-default-features` × release × debug) via `check_features.sh`, which derives the feature set from `Cargo.toml` (there is no `[features]` table, so default and `--no-default-features` are the whole space).\n\nBoth libraries are loaded only through `libloading` and called via `dlsym(\"driver\")` — the Rust `#[no_mangle]` wrapper is always exercised, never a direct Rust call.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n1. **The translation needed no fixes.** An independent cross-check — a standalone C program that `dlopen`s both `.so`s and sweeps 283,548 inputs (exhaustive low 16 bits, exhaustive per-byte positions, all single bits and complements, a strided full-32-bit sweep, and 200k seeded random values) — produced **identical SHA-256** for both outputs.\n\n2. **I fixed two problems in my own test infrastructure, not in the Rust:**\n   - `driver` reports via the process-wide libc `stdout`, so the harness must redirect fd 1. libtest's parallel progress text was landing inside the capture windows and causing 5 bogus failures. I switched the test targets to `harness = false` with a sequential runner reporting on stderr.\n   - My first `symbol_parity` check required the Rust `.so` to import `putchar`. That failed in debug builds — GCC and LLVM-at-`-O2` lower `printf(\"\\n\")` into `putchar('\\n')`, but LLVM at `-O0` does not. That is an optimizer detail, not an ABI or behavior difference, so I relaxed the assertion to require libc `printf` and documented why asserting on `putchar` would be testing the optimizer.\n\nTo guard against a vacuously-passing suite, I mutation-tested the harness with 8 injected divergences (signed-char promotion, wrong `bedrooms`/`bathrooms` constants, loop off-by-one, `%02X`, dropped newline, swapped struct field order, removed `#[no_mangle]`). **All 8 were killed**, and `src/lib.rs` was restored byte-identical afterward.\n\nNote: `cargo` had no network access, so builds used `--offline` against the cached `libloading 0.8.9`. `c_src/` was not modified. The only edit to existing files was `translation/Cargo.toml` (dev-dependency plus the three `harness = false` test targets)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":496,"cache_read_input_tokens":91440,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":496,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9bec4f7-4f99-4925-aa68-8e889adbff55","uuid":"aeebaca4-e3fc-47eb-aa58-d70a66331262","timestamp":"2026-08-28T16:17:43.271Z"}
